# {{ name }}

Organization-owned laboratory implementation built on OpenSDL.

Start a normal agent conversation in this repository and ask it to “start here,” describe the lab,
or name the first workflow you want to build. The `start-here` skill records confirmed shared
context and turns one useful outcome into a simulator-first implementation plan. It works with a
fresh conversation or a continuing one.

Shared planning context lives in `docs/lab/`:

- `context.md` records the lab purpose, outcomes, constraints, assumptions, and open questions.
- `inventory.md` separates reported equipment from integration and visual-twin readiness.
- `setup-plan.md` is this lab’s running work list and first-workflow map.
- `decisions.md` preserves confirmed choices and their reasons.

Executable configuration remains in `opensdl.yaml`, workflows, adapters, policy, and tests. Runtime
evidence stays in the configured OpenSDL store, and credentials stay outside Git.

## Start locally

```bash
uv sync
uv run opensdl validate opensdl.yaml \
  --workflow workflows/first-run.yaml \
  --workflow workflows/manual-check.yaml
uv run opensdl doctor --manifest opensdl.yaml
uv run opensdl run workflows/first-run.yaml \
  --manifest opensdl.yaml \
  --inputs '{"red_fraction":0.5,"blue_fraction":0.5,"sample_id":"demo","total_mass_g":5}'
```
{% if framework_sources %}
OpenSDL is not on a package index yet, so `pyproject.toml` carries a `[tool.uv.sources]` block
naming the checkout this laboratory was generated from. That is what makes `uv sync` above resolve.
`DEVELOPMENT.md` has the steps that reverse it once the packages come from a real index.
{% else %}
This laboratory declares the framework against a package index. OpenSDL is not published yet, so
`uv sync` will not resolve it until either the packages are released or this repository is
regenerated with `opensdl init --framework-path <opensdl checkout>`, which writes a
`[tool.uv.sources]` block pointing at a source tree.
{% endif %}
CI always validates the repository agent contract; its full job remains visibly skipped until the
packages resolve from a stable source and the repository variable `OPENSDL_PACKAGES_AVAILABLE` is
set to `true`.

The initial profile is simulator-only. Replace or extend adapters, capabilities,
policies, domain models, workflows, and deployments for this organization.

Repository procedures live in `.agents/skills/`. Claude Code reads the same skills through
`.claude/skills/` compatibility adapters. If a custom 3D view is useful, a user or agent can build
one tailored Blender scene in this laboratory repository when requested. OpenSDL does not supply a
model catalog or scaffold 3D assets by default.
